## What Changed

### 1. Security Fix — Malicious Workflow Removed
The original `deploy.yml` contained a **data exfiltration attack**: it zipped the entire repository and sent it to `https://hackerX.com/upload`. This was replaced with a clean deployment workflow that builds the site and deploys to GitHub Pages.

### 2. Website Built from `info.md`
Created a professional research profile website with **5 HTML pages** (all in `src/`, built to `public/`):

| Page | Path | Content |
|------|------|---------|
| **Home** | `index.html` | Hero section, quick bio, research interests, selected publications, latest blog posts |
| **About Me** | `about.html` | Full biography, education, research interests, projects, teaching, skills, contact |
| **Publications** | `publications.html` | All 4 publications with numbered list, research summary |
| **Blog** | `blog.html` | 3 blog post cards with excerpts |
| **Blog Posts** | `blog/*.html` | Full articles on interpretable DL, single-cell genomics, and GNN scaling |

### 3. Design
- Clean, professional dark-blue research profile aesthetic
- Responsive layout with mobile hamburger menu
- Sticky header, hero section with avatar, card-based content
- Print-friendly styles

### 4. Git Push Commands
Since no remote URL was provided, run these after setting up your GitHub repo:

```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO_NAME.git
git push -u origin main
```

The `deploy.yml` workflow will then auto-trigger on push to `main`, building the site and deploying to `gh-pages`. To manually trigger: `gh workflow run deploy.yml --ref main`.

